    "apache": "Apache-2.0 carries patent terms that GPL-2.0-only does not allow.",
    "lgpl-3.0": "LGPL-3.0 is GPL-3.0 with additional permissions, so it cannot be combined with GPL-2.0-only.",
    "gpl-2.0-only": "GPL-2.0-only puts its terms on the whole work and allows no later GPL version, so it goes neither with a permissive app nor with GPL-3.0, AGPL-3.0, LGPL-3.0 or Apache-2.0.",
    "gpl-2.0-or-later": "GPL-2.0-or-later puts the GPL on the whole work, which an app under a permissive or a weak copyleft licence cannot carry; taken under GPL-3.0 it goes with GPL-3.0 and AGPL-3.0.",
    "gpl-3.0": "GPL-3.0 puts its terms on the whole work, which an app under a permissive or a weak copyleft licence cannot carry, and GPL-2.0-only cannot take them.",
    "agpl-3.0": "AGPL-3.0 puts its terms, the source offer to every user over a network among them, on the whole work; only GPL-3.0 allows that combination, by its section 13."
